WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.685
Many notes still call the

2
00:00:01.685 --> 00:00:03.178
reverse repo the floor for

3
00:00:03.178 --> 00:00:04.154
short-term rates.

4
00:00:04.354 --> 00:00:06.423
Since 2022, it isn't.

5
00:00:06.923 --> 00:00:08.493
The RBI steers overnight

6
00:00:08.493 --> 00:00:09.867
rates with a corridor

7
00:00:09.967 --> 00:00:11.717
around its policy repo rate.

8
00:00:12.117 --> 00:00:13.718
The ceiling is the Marginal

9
00:00:13.718 --> 00:00:15.082
Standing Facility rate,

10
00:00:15.182 --> 00:00:16.867
a quarter point above repo.

11
00:00:17.267 --> 00:00:20.062
In April 2022, a new floor arrived:

12
00:00:20.182 --> 00:00:22.081
the Standing Deposit Facility,

13
00:00:22.181 --> 00:00:23.693
a quarter point below, with

14
00:00:23.693 --> 00:00:24.869
no collateral needed.

15
00:00:25.269 --> 00:00:26.691
The fixed-rate reverse repo

16
00:00:26.691 --> 00:00:27.850
stayed in the toolkit,

17
00:00:27.950 --> 00:00:29.422
but outside the corridor.

18
00:00:29.872 --> 00:00:31.792
As of October 2026:

19
00:00:31.892 --> 00:00:33.449
repo 5.5,

20
00:00:33.549 --> 00:00:36.152
deposit facility 5.25,

21
00:00:36.252 --> 00:00:39.004
MSF 5.75 percent.

22
00:00:39.454 --> 00:00:40.670
Learn the corridor,

23
00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:42.143
not just the rate.

24
00:00:42.643 --> 00:00:43.539
Your turn.

25
00:00:43.839 --> 00:00:45.439
Which facility is now the

26
00:00:45.439 --> 00:00:47.231
floor of the RBI's corridor?
